Package: richcast
Title: Hindcast Species Distributions and Assemblage Richness Through Time
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nimrod", "Marom", , "nxmarom@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits a species distribution model for every species near a
    region, projects it onto palaeoclimate reconstructions across a series of
    time slices, and stacks the results into assemblage richness surfaces.
    Ranges come from IUCN Red List polygons supplied by the user; each model
    is an equally weighted ensemble of a random forest and MaxEnt, trained on
    pseudo-presences sampled from the range polygon and evaluated by AUC and
    the continuous Boyce index. Climate data are retrieved via 'pastclim'. A
    trait table for rodents from Ecke et al. (2022)
    <doi:10.1038/s41467-022-35273-7> is bundled as a worked example.
